# scripts/check-agents-xref.ts audits skill citations of AGENTS.md sections, giving each a verdict: resolves, folio (a section handed to a folio) or unresolved.
# Each Scenario names the test that executes it.
Feature: AGENTS.md cross-reference audit

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::heading_and_name_matching::headings_are_read_at_every_level
  Scenario: Headings are read at every level
    Given markdown with "#", "##" and "####" headings and a line of text
    When headingsOf reads it
    Then it returns "a", "b" and "d"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::heading_and_name_matching::a_blockquoted_heading_is_a_heading
  Scenario: A blockquoted heading counts as a heading
    Given markdown with "> ## quoted" and ">### tight"
    When headingsOf reads it
    Then it returns "quoted" and "tight"
    And a "#" in the middle of a prose line is not read as a heading

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::heading_and_name_matching::this_repo's_own_banner_resolves,_not_just_a_fixture
  Scenario: The harness's own AGENTS.md banner and skill pointers resolve
    Given the harness's own AGENTS.md
    When its headings are read and normalised
    Then they include the "Do not edit this file to change how agents work" banner
    And they include "Getting skills"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::heading_and_name_matching::a_cited_name_matches_a_heading_that_carries_a_gloss_after_it
  Scenario: A cited name matches a heading that carries a gloss after it
    Given an AGENTS.md heading "Commit early, commit often, always PR (STRICT)"
    And a skill citing §"Commit early, commit often"
    When the citations are audited
    Then the single verdict is "resolves"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::heading_and_name_matching::normalise_strips_the_formatting_a_citation_and_a_heading_disagree_on
  Scenario: normalise strips the formatting a citation and a heading disagree on
    When normalise is applied to a string with padding, backticks and curly quotes
    Then the result is "foo — bar"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::the_third_state_—_a_section_this_file_hands_to_a_folio::an_attribution_that_WRAPS_across_lines_is_still_found
  Scenario: A folio attribution that wraps across lines is still found
    Given an AGENTS.md paragraph where the folio name ends one line and §"Branch + PR workflow" starts the next
    When folioAttributedSections reads it
    Then the attributed sections include "branch + pr workflow"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::the_third_state_—_a_section_this_file_hands_to_a_folio::a_citation_of_it_is_`folio`,_not_`unresolved`
  Scenario: A citation of a folio-attributed section is folio, not unresolved
    Given the wrapped attribution paragraph as AGENTS.md
    And a skill citing "Branch + PR workflow"
    When the citations are audited
    Then the single verdict is "folio"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::the_third_state_—_a_section_this_file_hands_to_a_folio::a_section_named_in_a_paragraph_with_no_folio_in_it_is_NOT_attributed
  Scenario: A section named in a paragraph with no folio in it is not attributed
    Given an AGENTS.md naming §"Some Other Thing" with no folio mentioned
    When folioAttributedSections reads it
    Then no section is attributed

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::unresolved::a_citation_naming_nothing_here_and_nothing_attributed_is_unresolved
  Scenario: A citation naming no heading here and nothing attributed is unresolved
    Given an AGENTS.md with only "Real heading"
    And a skill citing §"Critical-distance license"
    When the citations are audited
    Then the result is one "unresolved" citation of "Critical-distance license" in "skills/s.md"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::unresolved::a_bare_mention_of_AGENTS.md_naming_no_section_is_not_a_citation
  Scenario: A bare mention of AGENTS.md naming no section is not a citation
    Given a skill that mentions AGENTS.md without naming a section
    When the citations are audited
    Then no citation is reported

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::unresolved::a_missing_AGENTS.md_throws_rather_than_reporting_a_clean_run
  Scenario: A missing AGENTS.md throws rather than reporting a clean run
    Given an empty directory with no AGENTS.md
    When the citations are audited
    Then the audit throws

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::the_live_corpus::every_one_of_this_repo's_citations_gets_a_verdict,_and_none_is_unresolved
  Scenario: Every citation in the live harness corpus gets a verdict and none is unresolved
    Given the harness's own AGENTS.md and skill roots
    When the citations are audited
    Then no citation lacks a verdict
    And no citation is "unresolved"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::a_citation_may_declare_which_AGENTS.md_it_means::naming_another_repo_makes_it_`folio`_without_this_file_attributing_it
  Scenario: Naming another repo makes a citation folio without this file attributing it
    Given an AGENTS.md with only "Real heading"
    And a skill citing "litlfred/qou" AGENTS.md §"CI billing failures"
    When the citations are audited
    Then the single verdict is "folio"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::a_citation_may_declare_which_AGENTS.md_it_means::naming_THIS_repo_is_still_audited_against_this_file's_headings
  Scenario: Naming this repo still audits the citation against this file's headings
    Given an AGENTS.md titled for "litlfred/folio-assistant" with only "Real heading"
    And a skill citing "litlfred/folio-assistant" AGENTS.md §"Nope"
    When the citations are audited
    Then the single verdict is "unresolved"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-agents-xref.test.ts::a_citation_may_declare_which_AGENTS.md_it_means::qualifying_a_citation_moves_it_between_states_—_it_never_leaves_the_census
  Scenario: Qualifying a citation changes its verdict but never drops it from the census
    Given an AGENTS.md with only "Real heading"
    When a bare citation of §"Whatever" and a "litlfred/qou"-qualified one are audited separately
    Then both audits report the same number of citations
    And the bare citation is "unresolved"
    And the qualified citation is "folio"
